  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 158 PM EST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe extended period begins Wed morning as the developing frontal \nboundary to our west begins pushing precip into NW GA. By Wed \nmorning the frontal boundary is expected to be just to our west \nacross AL...but precipitation ahead of it will begin to push into \nNW GA just before daybreak Wed. As this front pushes into the \nregion it has to break down the High pressure ridge/wedge that is \nalready in place across the area. This ridge does a great job of \nslowing the Southeasterly progression of the frontal boundary \nwhich keeps precipitation chances elevated from 12z Wed to 12z Thu\nacross the state. Precipitable water values begin to increase Tue\nnight with values across West GA in the 1\" to 1.8\" range by 12z \nWed. These elevated PW values slowly traverse the area from W to E\nthrough Thur morning keeping precipitation chances high. Total \nQPF values are in the 1\" to 2\" range across a good portion of \nNorth and Central GA through Thu morning. Would not be surprised \nto see some isolated higher amounts closer to 2.5\" by Thu morning \nespecially across North GA. WPC has also put all of North GA and \nportions of Central GA under a day 3 ERO (Excessive Rain Outlook) \nfor this incoming system. \n\nThe better instability values and dynamics with this system stay \nwell north of the state along the front as it moves east through the \nMid-Atlantic states. Widespread severe weather is not expected. We \nwill see some isolated thunderstorms but for now not expecting much \nin the way of severe weather. \n\nThis front moves down into SE/S GA by Thu evening with another \nweaker/drier cold front expected to push into NW GA Fri evening and \nclearing things out for Sat. Should see mostly clear and slightly \ncooler conditions for the weekend .\n\nTemperatures will be mainly in the 70s to lower 80s through Friday \nwith highs cooling into the 60s and 70s Sat/Sun. Low temps expected \nin the 50s and 60s through Fri with lows in the 40s and 50s Sat/Sun. \nMay even see some upper 30s across the NE GA mountains Sun night.",
